Question 

 Kitto x demos are very desktop-like. Is there a way to make it look and feel more webby?

 Answer 

Looking very desktop-like is one of the original goals of Kitto x . The framework generates a full single-page application with tabs, modal dialogs, toolbars and grids that feel like a native desktop app. There is room for doing more web-like layouts through the use of templates. A TemplateDataPanel controller is available for displaying records using custom HTML templates as a grid replacement.

What you can do:

 Use the TemplateDataPanel controller for custom HTML-based record display;
 Embed views inside HTML pages through divs/css, frames or iframes;
 Conversely, host blocks of HTML inside views by means of the HtmlPanel controller;
 Customize the look and feel through CSS custom properties and the theme system.
